WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.800
In the eighth century, the Tang capital Chang'an was prosperous beyond compare.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.196
Its streets were packed with carts and horses — it was the liveliest city in the whole world at that time.

00:00:10.546 --> 00:00:16.500
But the burly military governor An Lushan harbored ambition in his heart.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:22.645
In the year 755, he raised the banner of revolt and rose in arms against the Tang.

00:00:22.995 --> 00:00:27.659
The great army set out, banners unfurled, dust and smoke rolling.

00:00:28.009 --> 00:00:32.357
On the distant horizon, thick black smoke rose up.

00:00:32.707 --> 00:00:37.112
The common people, supporting the old and leading the young, left their homes one after another.

00:00:37.462 --> 00:00:41.491
The great hall of the palace stood empty, with nothing left but silence.

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:45.711
Chang'an had fallen; its former prosperity was gone.

00:00:46.061 --> 00:00:51.977
The war lasted for years and brought enormous destruction to the Tang dynasty.

00:00:52.327 --> 00:00:55.498
From then on, the Tang dynasty turned from prosperity to decline.

00:00:55.848 --> 00:01:00.567
The An Lushan Rebellion became one of the most important turning points in Tang history.

